| PC-1 | CI wall time: run `linux-x86_64` in parallel with `test-matrix` where its work does not need it, split the CLI suite into shards, cache toolchains; update the stale "12–20 minutes" comment (decision D10: required check names and runner minutes) | median PR CI under 40 minutes with the same required-check semantics; measured over 20 runs | M | P0 |
| PC-2 | Leak and hang guard: a shared test helper that registers bridges, agents, gateways and child processes and fails the file at teardown if any survive; a per-file timeout in `run_tests.mjs`; a rule that lists test files constructing a bridge or agent without it (2 found, names to be captured first); also re-verify the stale/corrupt lock race and EXECUTION_CONVERGENCE I3/I4 from the old backlog and fix any defect found (accepted 2026-11-15) | the SI-2-style leak fails in 1 minute with the file name, not in 45 minutes; the re-verification result is recorded and any defect it shows is fixe
| PC-3 | Flake budget: record rerun-on-failure events, report weekly, fail when a test needs reruns twice in 20 runs | report committed as an artifact | S | P1 |
| PC-4 | Cross-runner reproducibility (22.04 vs 24.04) as a scheduled job, not a manual dispatch | job green; alert on drift | S | P2 |
| PC-5 | Opt-in crash and error reporting: confirm what OTLP does today (opt-in status unverified), document it, add a local crash report file under `~/.nexus/` | doc plus a test that nothing leaves the host without opt-in | S | P2 (settled by v1.3 GV-4; see docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md) |
| PC-6 | Dependency hygiene: `commander` major bump if safe, review the two Dependabot PRs, keep the no-deprecated gate | gate green | S | P2 |
| PC-7 | Flaky `eval_integrity` scanner test: `Python black-box oracle uses only pinned offline Go and Rust toolchains, or fails preflight` (the "more than 128 disjoint system roots" case) failed once on a loaded runner with `inventory enumeration_exit_batch_1_signal_sigterm` and passed on re-run; find what ends the enumeration (a time bound, a runner limit) and make the test independent of load, or give it a justified bound | passes 10 consecutive runs under artificial CPU load; any bound is documented in the test | S | P2 |

| DH-6 | Decide whether to switch `scripts/check_requirements.mjs` to enforce mode (the one open fragment of closed issue #7) and, if yes, bring the ledger rows to their accepted statuses | decision recorded; gate behaviour matches it | S | P2 |
